It is derived from the upstream branch
`u/oscarhiggott/fast-edge-reweighting-issue172` (commit 5fb9461f), not
from master. That branch already provided per-edge reweighting
(`edge_reweights`) for `Matching.decode` and `Matching.decode_batch`,
together with the initial tests in tests/matching/test_reweight.py.
Those are the work of the upstream authors, not of this fork.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Changes from upstream
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - Added a regularized reweight strength `alpha` to correlated matching.
    Where upstream applies hard Bayesian conditioning P(mu | nu), this fork
    applies implied_p = alpha * P(mu | nu). alpha=1.0 (the default) recovers
    the upstream behaviour exactly; alpha<1.0 softens the reweight and
    alpha>1.0 is permitted and not clamped. (Commits 4564c7f0, 69d7c049.)
  - Extended the existing per-edge reweighting (`edge_reweights`) to
    `Matching.decode_to_edges_array`, which the base branch did not cover.
    (Commit c581d641.)
  - Cached the implied-weight table per alpha rather than recomputing it
    per shot. (Commit 4b3d3720.)
  - Extended tests/matching/test_reweight.py with cases covering alpha.

